#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:210
#: 367fdcd7910e455aa68475f4ba2b784d
msgid "The board has two dedicated power monitor ports on 6 pin connectors, one for an analog monitor and one for a DroneCAN monitor. The correct battery setting parameters are dependent on the type of power brick which is connected. By default, use of a DroneCAN battery monitor is enabled by default as the first battery monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:213
#: e90b461869284997976e5bed3021efc0
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:214
#: cb04cce6b4284b52a11179a9f526603d
msgid "The RCIN pin, which by default is mapped to a timer input, can be used for all ArduPilot supported unidirectional receiver protocols. Bi-directional protocols such as CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 require a full UART connection. FPort, when connected to RCIN, will only provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:216
#: 67613b3e2b3646d4a1d2cc3bd274c7bc
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, a full UART, such as SERIAL6 (UART7) would need to be used for receiver connections. Below are setups using Serial6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:218
#: 7a4a93fda92644f6bb55051794dc5185
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL6_PROTOCOL<SERIAL6_PROTOCOL>` should be set to \"23\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:219
#: 162abfe460d74b629f337a986677cd4a
msgid "FPort would require :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` be set to \"15\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:220
#: 4eb556a4e165407891896987dcafa7a4
msgid "CRSF would require :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` be set to \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:221
#: c4def7a2c61c4e678565b8166ac99120
msgid "SRXL2 would require :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` be set to \"4\" and connects only the TX pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-NarinFC-H7.rst:223
#: 2d44a46962c947cc889f6749eb3cb342
msgid "Any UART can also be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM. See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details. The power rail associated with this connector position is powered either via USB or PMU."
msgstr ""

